d  Sciences the Academy for short if you  think the long name sounds snooty that's  the whole point  according to Thompson it made you think  the Academy had always been there  arranged by God and Harvard and Albert  Einstein and not a few cigar smoking  jerks looking for cheap non-union labor  at its inception the Academy was  comprised of 36 actors directors writers  technicians and producers they were  conferred elite status and the vague  promise that working conditions in the  industry would improve but while the  Academy promised to create industry  standards and handle labor disputes it  was privately viewed as a way to render  unions unnecessary on a broader level  the organization was dedicated to  promoting a positive wholesome image of  Hollywood there  a decade plagued by industry scandals in  the form of Charlie Chaplin and  scandalous divorce or fatty Arbuckle's  being tried for drunken manslaughter  anyway these powerful image conscious  folks had a fancy banquet in January of  1927 the only thing the festivities were  missing something to make people feel  even more special a legitimizing factor  if you will enter awards as mayor  accounted to his biographer I found that  the best way to handle movie makers was  to hang medals all over them if I got  them cups and awards they'd kill  themselves to produce what I wanted  that's why the Academy Award was created  come 1929 the first awards were handed  out in a 15 minute private ceremony  these awards were also a way for the  movie industry to affirm its own  artistic importance on one level this  can seem as obvious self-indulgence on  another level scholar Peter de tourny  argues it was a way to brand Hollywood  talent as skilled artistry rather than  labour in the process rendering labor  unions unnecessary dieter nee argues  that the award categories themselves  created two separate classes of  Hollywood workers lowly laborers and  artistes however mayor's ingenious  solution to the pesky union pro